{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1130,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mirrors are amazing - they turn walls into\nportals to another world!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5940,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, our world, only slightly different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8740,
    "dDurationMs": 3670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, you’ve probably noticed that words\nlook backwards in a mirror, but they aren’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12410,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "upside down - which is weird, because how\nwould a mirror know to flip left and right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16400,
    "dDurationMs": 1089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but not up and down?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17489,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the short, annoying answer is that mirrors\ndon’t flip left and right OR up and down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22029,
    "dDurationMs": 3931,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- if you look carefully at a scene in a mirror,\nyou’ll notice that everything on the left"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25960,
    "dDurationMs": 4229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stays on the left, everything on the right\nstays on the right, everything up stays up,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30189,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and everything down stays down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32559,
    "dDurationMs": 4521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What does get flipped is the direction into\nor out of the mirror - the things closest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37080,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to us end up farthest away, and the things\nfarthest from us end up closest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42140,
    "dDurationMs": 6290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mirrors flip not left and right, nor up and\ndown, but depth - they flip in and out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48430,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And mirrors invert in and out because they\nreflect light according to the principle of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52170,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specular reflection: light coming into the\nmirror at a given angle bounces back out at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56510,
    "dDurationMs": 1100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same angle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57610,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This means that, after bouncing off a mirror,\nlight is behaving no differently than it would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61350,
    "dDurationMs": 3919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have if instead of a mirror there were a window\ninto a parallel universe on the other side,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65269,
    "dDurationMs": 3191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like ours in every way except with in\nand out reversed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68460,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s why mirrors feel like windows into\nanother world - the light is behaving in LITERALLY"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73700,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same way as it would if they WERE windows\ninto another world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76840,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, but then what about the left-right flip\nquestion?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80100,
    "dDurationMs": 2839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How does that make sense if mirrors DON’T\nflip left and right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82939,
    "dDurationMs": 3651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, you can literally see the answer for\nyourself by writing on something transparent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86590,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- when the word is readable left-to-right,\nits mirror image is also readable left to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91170,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92170,
    "dDurationMs": 3579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reason words are usually flipped in mirrors\nisn’t because mirrors flip them; WE flip"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95749,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96749,
    "dDurationMs": 2791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Words, it turns out, tend to be printed on\nor attached to objects that we have to turn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99540,
    "dDurationMs": 2429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to face the mirror in order to see in the\nmirror."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101969,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "WE flip the words - and we normally do it\nleft \u0026 right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104749,
    "dDurationMs": 3021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We could just as well turn them vertically,\nin which case the word would look flipped"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107770,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "top-bottom in the mirror, not left-right!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109939,
    "dDurationMs": 1901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, not the mirror’s doing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111840,
    "dDurationMs": 4419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here’s the deal: if a word is flipped in\na mirror, it’s probably flipped outside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116259,
    "dDurationMs": 1051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the mirror, too!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117310,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We just don’t normally notice that the word\ngot flipped outside because we can’t see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120390,
    "dDurationMs": 1609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through solid objects."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121999,
    "dDurationMs": 3421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In order to see the word without looking in\nthe mirror, we have to go around to the other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125420,
    "dDurationMs": 3059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "side of the object and turn ourselves around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128479,
    "dDurationMs": 4951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unless you have multiple mirrors - in that\ncase, in and out get flipped along two different"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133430,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "directions, which combines to mean that things\non the left indeed show up on the right and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138790,
    "dDurationMs": 5740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right on the left - or, if we rotate the mirrors,\nup gets flipped with down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144530,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if somebody tells you mirrors don’t flip\nleft and right - well, mirrORS actually CAN"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149420,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- but not mirrOR."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150700,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lone, single mirror has to get us to do\nthe flipping for it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155920,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, before you flip channels, I’ve got\na channel recommendation for you: MinuteBody."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160810,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wait, but I thought this video was sponsored\nby CuriosityStream, which has teamed up with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164770,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nebula, a new streaming service featuring\noriginal videos from independent and education-y"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168570,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "youtube creators?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169970,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well yes it is - and those original series\ninclude MinuteBody, produced by the MinuteEarth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174200,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "team, or “The Logistics of D-Day” produced\nby Real Engineering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177500,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can get Nebula for free bundled with\na CuriosityStream subscription by going to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181670,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "curiositystream.com/minutephysics, which gets\nyou access to the thousands of documentaries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186460,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on CuriosityStream AND all of Nebula for just\n$20 a year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190750,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So go to curiositystream.com/minutephysics\nand you can watch Particle Fever, MinuteBody,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195280,
    "dDurationMs": 1540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "AND the logistics of D-day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196820,
    "dDurationMs": 1669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, and new MinutePhysics videos are there\ntoo, in case you want to watch without ads."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198489,
    "dDurationMs": 4481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to CuriosityStream and Nebula for supporting\neducational videos on the internet!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
